# UORC — Universal Object Reference Compression

A lossless compression system whose compressed object is an exact executable Universal Object Reference synthesized under explicit accounting and evidence.

## Current status

The first product generation is v0.1 and includes the complete compression product. Current development source composes framing, reference and runtime semantics, deterministic synthesis, accounting, evidence, and user operations. Release acceptance requires the complete current graph and generated products to pass their declared checks. Source presence or a partial diagnosimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import {readFile, writeFile} from 'node:fs/promises';

// Initial bootstrap binds the real selected SDK bytes. An existing project's
// standards choice requires explicit review; never silently replace it.
export async function bindStandardsLock(path, expected) {
  let existing;
  try { existing = await readFile(path); }
  catch (error) { if (error.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error; }
  if (existing !== undefined) {
    assert.deepEqual(existing, expected, 'existing standards.lock differs from the selected SDK; review the standards change explicitly');
  } else {
    await writeFile(path, expected, {flag: 'wx'});
  }
}
