## Executed procedure

`just integrity` runs the unfiltered importer/harness tests and
`scripts/integrity-validation.mjs`. It is required by the existing complete
`just vv`, which retains every earlier prerequisite. The harness verifies the
source, plants both source-owned arithmetic/length defects, checks the exact
owning generated theorem location, verifies restored controls, then builds and
executes the generated Lean model against every locked vector. It has no
handwritten hash implementation or production fallback. The generated client
also checks 2,919 partitions, SHA-256 abc, finalization/error behavior,<!-- uorc:non-authoritative -->
# RuntimeImage adapter checkpoint

Own and Archive use the shared RuntimeImage interface for image validation and reads. The source-owned ImageAccessControls module calls the actual adapters and producer spans. Charged APIs preserve the work performed before typed failure; plain APIs project the result. On success the charged work equals Transition.work and is charged once.

The retained producer image ticket remains a root until consumption and release. RuntimeImage descriptors are borrowed and never pin an image. Empty spans perform no image access. Error prefixes include attempted access, retained heap work, and admitted byte materialization.

The adjacent evidence manifest binds current adapter sources. Saved native execution passed 20 independent fixtures, 60 partitions, 10 owned reconstructions, paired success work, typed failure prefixes, digest early/late mismatch, and complete valid-root cleanup. The control-payload rejection deliberately forges an invalid snapshot: Heap prevents creating it, so this case makes no valid-arena claim.

The same OwnedLifecycleLaws module is now replaced with 27 main proof roots and 33 native declarations against the actual RuntimeImage adapter. Its equations include successful charged read work, failed read prefixes, failed child admission, and work normalization. Archive reads require the actual prefix-byte admission condition. The prior ticket, update, release acknowledgment, drain, cancelled stability, and digest publication laws remain. Native source compilation, all-declaration axiom audit, and leanchecker replay passed. Dependencies use only propext and Quot.sound where declared; no custom axiom or Classical dependency was added.

Two isolated defects establish failure: changing the ready-step one-byte theorem type to two bytes is kernel-rejected; changing only acceptedByteCharged report copy-count from one to two compiles as adapter source but invalidates acceptedByte_unfold. Restoring the exact adapter in the same model makes proof compilation and leanchecker pass. Private Lean producer/exporter helpers remain outside the repository; the checked-in native LexLean proof is authoritative.

This checkpoint does not establish complete scoped SDK closure. The old OwnedLifecycleLaws receipt (32671bba lineage) used the previous Own/RuntimeSequence read boundary and remains historical. The replacement source and its native receipts are separately bound in the current evidence manifest.

An actual complete 19-module run found 39 missing UInt64 foundation declarations across Own and Archive. All 97 computational/control declarations were traced, and only those exact axiom fields were corrected to `Quot.sound` and `propext`; bodies, signatures and runtime behavior are unchanged. The corrected run passes all source-policy audits, retains all 16 Core production roots and unchanged limits, then rejects certificate A `LexLeanPreserve.C2225d74ba422e93f70040c4291cac47a.R14.__rel_16` for `Uorc.Uorc.Core.Heap.releaseStep` with `LLV7013`, kernel deep recursion. This current failure is distinct from the prior RuntimeSequence failure. Both original policy failure and corrected complete run are preserved under `sdk-policy`. No compiler policy, lock or limit was changed.

